Mastering Propositional Logic & Truth Tables
Complete Beginner-to-Application Roadmap

✅ 1. Learn the Basic Logical Operators
These are essential to all logical expressions:

Symbol	Name	Meaning
∧	Conjunction	AND — True if both are True
∨	Disjunction	OR — True if at least one is True
¬	Negation	NOT — Reverses truth value
⊕	Exclusive OR	XOR — True if only one is True
→	Implication	IF P THEN Q — False only if P is True and Q is False
↔	Bi-conditional	IF AND ONLY IF — True if both are same

